<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Quraysh</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Quraysh were the dominant Arab tribe of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a>, to which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prophet-muhammad">Prophet Muhammad</a> belonged. Its Umayyad clan initially opposed Muhammad before his victory in 630 CE. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muawiya-i">Muawiyah</a> of this clan founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a>, turning the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphate</a> into a hereditary monarchy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/quraysh.jpg" alt="Quraysh" width="320" height="267" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SPQR10 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pre_Islamic_Arabian_Tribes_(Harold_Dixon).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
